{
  "name": "Paintrz — Guest Links",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Guest links (QR handover)\n\nThree endpoints for the homeowner's own phone. A guest has **no Supabase session**, and both `storage.objects` and `renders` are behind RLS keyed on `auth.uid()` — so a guest can write to neither. Every write here happens on the service role.\n\n- `paintrz-guest-info` — is this token alive, and whose brand is it?\n- `paintrz-guest-render` — accept a photo, start a render\n- `paintrz-guest-status` — poll one render, scoped to the token\n\n### This does NOT re-implement the render pipeline\nIt prepares the row and calls **Paintrz — Render Pipeline** over HTTP. One pipeline, one place to fix.\n\n### Before this works\n1. Run `sql/guest-links.sql` in Supabase.\n2. Create the **Paintrz Supabase service role** custom-auth credential and attach it to every HTTP node here.\n3. Publish, then confirm the three Production URLs match `CONFIG.N8N_GUEST_*` in app.html.",
        "height": 460,
        "width": 420
      },
      "id": "note_overview",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-2600, -720]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## CORS\nThese are POSTs with `Content-Type: application/json`, so the browser sends a **preflight OPTIONS** first — unlike the colours proxy, which is a simple GET and needs only a response header.\n\n`allowedOrigins` on each Webhook node is what answers that preflight. The `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header on each Respond node covers the actual response.\n\nIf preflight still fails, the n8n build is too old for `allowedOrigins`; the fallback is to post as `text/plain` and parse the body server-side.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 380
      },
      "id": "note_cors",
      "name": "CORS note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-2600, -230]
    },

