    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Why the count is spent AFTER the render\nThe cap is charged only once the pipeline reports success, so a failed render does not eat the homeowner's allowance. The trade-off is a small race: several guests submitting at the same instant can each pass validation. `consume_guest_render` increments inside its own guard, so the stored count still cannot exceed the cap — at worst a render or two slips through.\n\nCharging up front would close that, at the cost of burning the cap on every failure. Given the pipeline has never yet completed a render, that is the worse trade today. Revisit once it is proven.",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 400
      },
      "id": "note_consume",
      "name": "Consume note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [520, -60]
    },

